    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1221">

                <pb facs="1212" n="926" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg926"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.142/1494</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 27, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 4.50 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4041. Your 3036, March 14. Foreign Office replies that, as medical supplies are
                    apparently to be delivered to Turkish officials on the quay, it will be
                    necessary before considering application to have information as to how it is
                    intended to insure that stores so landed reach Jewish hospitals for which they
                    are destined.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1221-f1"/> Foreign Office also states it
                    will be necessary that application should also be addressed to French
                    Government, and I am replying that this has been done.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1221-f1" n="2" xml:id="d1221-f1-content">
                <p>This statement transmitted to the Chargé in Turkey by telegram No. 2172, March
                    29, 1916.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
